From 5cc00610e91588e0363af172b35241a7c8fc99f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julia Klee <71413974+kleeedolinux@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:42:27 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] lib: wolos_bend, work-stealing fork/join and lock-free pools

Small parallel primitives with no runtime of their own:
- bend_meet()/bend_subst(): two parties meet at a slot with one CAS
- bend_deque: Chase-Lev deque; a thief claims up to 4 entries with one
  CAS, the owner pops without a CAS only while out of every claim's reach
- bend_arena: per-worker bump allocator, freed in one call
- bend_pool: objects reused by index, generation-checked handles,
  tagged free-list head against ABA
- bend_fork_join(): split until the grain, helpers on idle CPUs (same
  LLC first) through a per-CPU workqueue, the caller works too
- bend_clear_user_highpages(): the first user, clears a large user folio
  in pieces (wolos_bend.clear_min_kb, clear_grain_kb)

wolos_bend.enable=0 makes every fork/join serial. KUnit wolos_bend runs
the concurrent cases on every CPU (UML: ncpus=4 seccomp=on).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
